From f0c0b3bde1adf7136efee265b94fc25af6009dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:53:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: cell identity consistency detector
 (T-OR-059)

CellConsistencyAnalyzer (default off, `cell_consistency`) flags an E-UTRAN
cell that advertises the same identity (ECGI) with two different tracking
area codes within one recording -- possible identity cloning or tracking-area
rotation by a false base station. Corroborative -> Low; fires once per cell.

The cell key is the full ECGI (primary PLMN MCC+MNC plus the 28-bit
cellIdentity), because cellIdentity is only unique within a PLMN, so two PLMNs
can legitimately share one cellIdentity (fixes cross-PLMN false positives).
Identifiers are unpacked to integers (not hashed BitVec bytes) and the state
maps are bounded (4096 cells) against untrusted SIB1 broadcast floods.

Scope is SIB1-only and sound without real-capture calibration. Correlating the
ECGI with the serving PCI (an ML1 measurement) is deferred to T-OR-118: a
serving measurement cannot be reliably attributed to a cell across idle-mode
reselection without the per-SIB1 PCI or calibrated hysteresis, so doing it now
would false-positive on routine mobility.

Privacy: compares the ECGI and TAC but never puts either in an event.

Test vectors are SIB1 PDUs encoded with pycrate and decoded through
telcom_parser: same ECGI with two TACs (fires once), with one TAC (quiet),
two different cellIdentities (quiet), and the same cellIdentity under two PLMNs
(quiet -- legal).

